this is newly released body cam footage  of the response to the attack at robb  elementary school in uvalde  nearly 400 officers were called to the  school but they failed to take any  action for more than an hour  the shooter killed 19 students and two  teachers before he was confronted by  by police and killed mike hanna reports  if there's only one thing that i can  tell you is  there were multiple systemic failures  the three members of the bipartisan  texas house committee held a news  conference to discuss the report  it comes just a few days after this new  security camera footage was released  the sounds of the children screaming are  edited out but it shows local police  arriving two minutes after the shooting  started  a few approach the classroom door but  then retreat back down the corridor  after shots are fired  the report is adamant that during this  time officers at a federal or state  level should have taken over control  from the school police chief pete  arredondo who was supposedly in charge  at the school  today teredondo has taken much of the  blame but sunday's report says  responsibility for the lack of action  should be shared by some of the 376 law  enforcement officers who had arrived as  well as their superiors at a command  level at a minimum  there is multiple opportunities  depending on the relative training and  experience of law enforcement officers  to at least ask more questions or offer  their guidance to try to remedy the  chaotic situation and make sure there is  effective overall command there was a  lack of effective overall command that  day  the report also found the school's  safety protocols fell far short numerous  doors were left unlocked which allowed  the gunman easy access to the classrooms  in a wider context the legislators also  found that these issues were not unique  to the ross elementary school where the  shooting happened  that protocols not observed created a  dangerous sense of false security let me  tell you the people of uvalde before  this  they felt it couldn't happen here  they felt that that's the false sense of  security i worry about i think some of  the same systems  that we found here that failed that day  are across the entire state and country  the report is dedicated to the 21  victims of the shooting and was given to  family and friends at a meeting an hour  before its public release  a report that drove home the tragic fact  that law enforcement officials waited  for some 75 minutes while gunfire  continued  before a group of border patrol guards  to fight orders on the scene and rushed  in to kill the gunman  mike hannah al-jazeera washington
 

